---
import DetailLayout from "../../layouts/DetailLayout.astro";
---

<DetailLayout
  title="Meili Snow Mountain"
  description="Meili Snow Mountain, Shangri-La Yunnan: sacred Kawagebo peak at 6,740m. Sunrise at Feilai Temple, transport, best season, and trekking routes."
  category="Attraction"
  image="meili-snow-mountain.webp"
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "TouristAttraction",
    "name": "Meili Snow Mountain",
    "description": "Sacred mountain range including Kawagebo (6,740m), Yunnan's highest peak. Iconic sunrise views from Feilai Temple are one of China's most spectacular landscapes.",
    "publicAccess": true
  }}
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Meili Snow Mountain</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-500">Sacred to Tibetan Buddhists. Kawagebo at 6,740m is Yunnan's highest peak and has never been climbed. The sunrise view from Feilai Temple is one of China's most iconic landscapes.</p>

  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Altitude</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">6,740 m (peak)</span></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Time Needed</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">1&ndash;2 days</span></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Best Season</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">Oct&ndash;May</span></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Ticket</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">Free (viewing)</span></div>
  </div>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Overview</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Meili Snow Mountain (u6885u91ccu96eau5c71) is a sacred mountain range straddling the border of northwest Yunnan and Tibet. Its highest peak, <strong>Kawagebo</strong> (6,740m), is the tallest mountain in Yunnan Province and the spiritual heart of Tibetan Buddhism in the region. Every year, thousands of Tibetan pilgrims circumambulate the range on foot in an act of devotion that can take 10&ndash;15 days.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Kawagebo is one of the few major peaks in the world that has never been summited. A 1991 Sino-Japanese expedition ended in tragedy when all 17 climbers perished in an avalanche. The mountain has been closed to climbing attempts since 2001, preserving its untainted mystique.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">For most visitors, the experience centers on the sunrise viewpoint at <strong>Feilai Temple</strong> (3,400m), about 4 hours by car from Shangri-La. As the sun rises, the snow-covered peaks of the Meili range turn from pale blue to pink to blazing gold &mdash; a phenomenon called "Golden Mountain Sunrise." It is one of the most spectacular natural sights in China and the reason travelers make the long drive from Shangri-La.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">How to Get There</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 space-y-5">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">From Shangri-La by Car (Recommended)</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">The drive from Shangri-La to Feilai Temple takes <strong>3.5&ndash;4 hours</strong> via National Highway G214. The road climbs over Baima Snow Mountain pass (4,292m) with stunning views. Hire a Tibetan-speaking driver for <strong>600&ndash;800 RMB</strong> round trip. The road conditions are good but mountain weather can cause delays.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">By Bus</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Daily buses from Shangri-La Bus Station to Deqin County (the nearest town) depart at 9:00 AM. Journey is 5&ndash;6 hours, fare <strong>60&ndash;80 RMB</strong>. From Deqin, take a local minibus or taxi 10 km to Feilai Temple (20&ndash;30 RMB).</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Where to Stay &amp; Eat</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600"><strong>Feilai Temple village</strong> has a strip of guesthouses and small hotels facing the Meili range. The best rooms have windows oriented toward Kawagebo for sunrise viewing from bed. Prices range from <strong>150&ndash;400 RMB</strong> per night. Book ahead during October&ndash;November peak season. Restaurants in Feilai Temple serve Tibetan and Sichuan food: hotpot (80&ndash;150 RMB for two), noodle soups (15&ndash;25 RMB), yak dishes (40&ndash;70 RMB). The nearby town of Deqin has more dining options including fresh local walnuts and Tibetan barley wine.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Sunrise Viewing Tips</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span><strong>Set your alarm for 6:30 AM.</strong> Sunrise is around 7:00&ndash;7:30 AM depending on season. The golden light peaks for about 10 minutes.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span>The best months for clear skies are <strong>October through December</strong>. Summer monsoon (June&ndash;August) often obscures the peaks in clouds.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span>Dress warmly &mdash; even in spring, Feilai Temple at 3,400m is cold at dawn (0&ndash;5u00b0C).</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span><strong>Be patient.</strong> If clouds obscure the peaks in the morning, they sometimes clear by 9:00 AM. Stay for a second cup of yak butter tea.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 p-6">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-emerald-700">Nearby &raquo;</p>
    <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <a href="/attractions/tiger-leaping-gorge" class="rounded-full bg-white border border-slate-200 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-slate-700 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-700 transition-colors">Tiger Leaping Gorge</a>
      <a href="/attractions/balagezong-canyon" class="rounded-full bg-white border border-slate-200 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-slate-700 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-700 transition-colors">Balagezong Canyon</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</DetailLayout>